  "tagline": "Embedded Java hypergraph database where edges can link any number of atoms, including other edges.",
  "description": "HyperGraphDB is an open-source, embeddable Java database built on a generalized hypergraph: every stored item is an atom, and links can point to any number of atoms, including other links. That makes it suited to knowledge representation, AI and semantic-web research where n-ary and higher-order relations are first-class. It stores data on BerkeleyDB Java Edition, includes a type system that maps Java objects directly, and offers peer-to-peer replication. The last formal release is 1.3, and development is sporadic (a burst of fixes in October 2026 after years of quiet), so it fits research rather than production.",
